Write the full `plan.md` document from the accepted spec and design.

{% set document = "plan.md" %}{% include "_document_contract.md" %}

{% include "_repos.md" %}

**Slice vertically.** Each task should deliver a working, testable path through
the system — not "build all the schema", then "build all the API". A task that
leaves nothing demonstrable is the wrong slice.

**Order by dependency, and put the risky work first.** Build the foundation
before what stands on it, keep the system working after every task, and learn
what is most likely to change the plan early rather than late.

Give every task this shape:

```markdown
## Task N: <short descriptive title>

**Description:** One paragraph on what this task accomplishes.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- [ ] Specific, testable condition
- [ ] Specific, testable condition

**Verification:** The repository's own focused test and build commands, plus any
manual check.

**Dependencies:** Task numbers, or None.

**Files likely touched:** Real paths in this repository.

**Scope:** Small (1-2 files) | Medium (3-5) | Large (5+)
```

Put an explicit checkpoint after every two or three tasks: what must pass, and
what a human should look at before the plan continues.

{% if jira %}
Documentation work belongs inside the task that makes it necessary, not in a
task of its own at the end: a task that changes behaviour carries its own
document update, and its acceptance criteria say so. The task list covers: `doc/spec-{{ jira }}.md`
when issue context, scope or acceptance criteria change; `doc/design-{{ jira }}.md`
for API, data-model, pipeline, deployment or cross-repo decisions;
`doc/usage-{{ jira }}.md` for changed setup, behaviour, commands, rollout,
operations or support; and, as ship-time work
rather than part of this change, a refresh of
`doc/release-approval-{{ jira }}.evidence.json`. For a Java
repo, include the compile, test, style, static-analysis and Alibaba
Mandatory-rule verification tasks.

{% endif %}Close with a coverage matrix proving the plan covers the documents it came from.
A plan is not ready until every acceptance criterion and every design decision
maps to a task, and anything deliberately uncovered says so:

```markdown
## Requirement Coverage
| Source | Requirement or decision | Covered by | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| spec | <acceptance criterion> | Task 2, Task 5 | |
| design | <decision> | Task 3 | |
```

